.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_GET0_UIDS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_get0_uids ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_get0_issuerUID
.Nd get certificate and attribute certificate unique identifiers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft void
.Fo X509_get0_uids
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_BIT_STRING **piuid"
.Fa "const ASN1_BIT_STRING **psuid"
.Fc
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft ASN1_BIT_STRING *
.Fo X509_ACERT_get0_issuerUID
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fc
.Bd -literal
=head1 DESCRIPTION
.Ed
.Fn X509_get0_uids
sets
.Nm *piuid
and
.Ar *psuid
to the issuer and subject unique identifiers of certificate
.Ar x
or NULL if the fields are not present.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_issuerUID
returns the issuer unique identifier of the attribute certificate
.Ar x
or NULL if the field is not present.
.Sh NOTES
The issuer and subject unique identifier fields are very rarely
encountered in practice outside test cases.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_get0_uids
does not return a value.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_issuerUID
returns a unique identifier on success or NULL on failure.
